cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research record, its data or its benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "RatLab — A Boar Research: an offline phone research assistant measured against 'half as good as internet plus a frontier AI' (research record v1.1.2)"
abstract: >-
  The research record of BOAR, an offline Android research assistant built for poidh bounty #31
  ("more than 50 % as good as internet plus a frontier AI", at most 12 GB RAM, English), and of LabRat
  (formerly BoarLite), the app submitted to it. Record version 1.1.2, as of 2026-10-28; the author closed the
  research lines on 2026-10-23. It covers two benchmarks (frozen frontier-plus-web references, a pairwise LLM judge
  in both presentation orders, pre-registered pass/fail rules; a second 75-item ruler written half by each judge
  family), 387 recorded experiments in the public registry (215 of them ended without a gain), the decision log and
  the standing. The bar was not reached as of 2026-10-28: on a Pixel 8a in airplane mode LabRat won 0 of 71
  head-to-heads under both judge families on the second ruler (bench v0.4, two seeds), with U-total 0.165 under
  Claude Opus and 0.242 under OpenAI gpt-5.6-sol. Criteria, arm reports, aggregates and tools are in boar-research,
  the benchmark and every evaluation set in boar-bench, and the raw run traces and judgments in boar-traces.
  Health material is AI-reviewed, not clinically reviewed.
